ocratic lean.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 72 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District features a rematch between Republican incumbent Jen Kiggans and Democrat Elaine Luria, who held the seat before losing it in 2022. The district is evenly split partisan terrain, and the race centers on health care, affordability, and national issues. Luria has raised heavily and drawn outside support, while Kiggans holds the advantages of incumbency and comparable cash on hand.\n\nRaters are divided: some call the race a tossup, while others place it in the Lean or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets price Luria's chances around 80 percent. The only available poll, from July, showed the candidates tied. The overall picture is a competitive race with a modest Democratic edge, consistent with a Lean D rating and meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}]}